file: "packages/core/src/delta/recolor_shape.ts"
doc:
  "Applies the diff treatment to the two glyph types: every colour they carry, plus ghosting on deletion.\n"
  "\n"
  "Vocabulary for this file is fixed in delta_overlay.spec.textproto.\n"
  "\n"
  "GHOSTING is the extra treatment a DELETED element gets, applied in both\n"
  "table mode and rotate mode. It is defined per glyph type, and the two types\n"
  "do different amounts of it: recolorShape performs two edits on a Glyph2D,\n"
  "recolorLine performs one on a Glyph1D. Each decl below states its own,\n"
  "and there is no count that governs both.\n"
  "\n"
  "Neither function reads a theme or a token. Both take an already-chosen\n"
  "DiffRoles (or undefined) and hand it straight to diffColorFor."

methods: [
  { name: "recolorShape"
    doc:
      "A copy of `glyph` with the diff treatment applied. `glyph` is not\n"
      "mutated.\n"
      "\n"
      "Every colour the glyph carries is replaced by diffColorFor of its\n"
      "current value, in four places:\n"
      "  stroke.color             (only when stroke.paint is the color case)\n"
      "  fill.color               (only when fill.paint is the color case)\n"
      "  glow.color\n"
      "  decorations[].color      every entry that sets one\n"
      "An unset optional is left unset -- no colour is invented for a field\n"
      "the theme did not fill.\n"
      "\n"
      "A stroke or fill whose paint is the GRADIENT case is left exactly as\n"
      "it is, and no colour is derived from it. A gradient has no single hue\n"
      "to rotate and no single value to replace. No bundled theme uses one\n"
      "today, so this path is untested by the bundled renders.\n"
      "\n"
      "GHOSTING, when and only when `change` is DELETED -- two edits:\n"
      "  stroke.dashing is set to STROKE_PATTERN_DOTTED, discarding whatever\n"
      "    dashing it had. If the glyph has no stroke at all, no stroke is\n"
      "    created.\n"
      "  fill.opacity is set to its current value multiplied by 0.4. A Fill\n"
      "    that is present with `opacity` unset counts as 1.0, so it becomes\n"
      "    0.4. If the glyph has NO fill at all, no Fill is created and no\n"
      "    opacity is set -- an absent fill stays absent.\n"
      "For every other change type, dashing and opacity are left untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "The opacity edit is computed FROM the prior value; the dashing edit\n"
      "discards it. They are asymmetric on purpose, and the reason is what\n"
      "the bundled themes already set. Group components ship already dashed\n"
      "(customDasharray \"5,4\") at fill opacity 0.06. A fixed opacity of 0.25\n"
      "would render a deleted group four times MORE solid than an unchanged\n"
      "one, so opacity has to scale. DOTTED needs no scaling because it is\n"
      "already distinct both from a solid node outline and from that \"5,4\".\n"
      "\n"
      "CARRIED THROUGH UNTOUCHED, in full: shape_kind (both the standard and\n"
      "custom_path_ref cases), corner_radius, stroke.width, stroke.cap,\n"
      "stroke.join, glow.radius, glow.intensity, decorations[].id,\n"
      "decorations[].kind, decorations[].badge_text, decorations[].icon_ref\n"
      "and decorations[].position. This function changes colours, one dash\n"
      "pattern and one opacity, and nothing else -- no geometry and no size.\n"
      "\n"
      "Ghosting matters beyond looks: it is the only channel that still\n"
      "separates DELETED from ADDED when hue is disregarded, which is the\n"
      "case for a red-green colourblind reader in table mode and for a fully\n"
      "desaturated palette in rotate mode."
    inputs: [
      { name: "glyph",     type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.style.v1.Glyph2D" } } },
      { name: "change",    type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } } },
      { name: "diffRoles", type: { named: { symbol: "DiffRoles" } }, is_optional: true }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.style.v1.Glyph2D" } }
    uses: ["diffColorFor", "archeglyph.style.v1.StrokePattern"]
  },
  { name: "recolorLine"
    doc:
      "A copy of `glyph` with the diff treatment applied. `glyph` is not\n"
      "mutated.\n"
      "\n"
      "Every colour the glyph carries is replaced by diffColorFor of its\n"
      "current value, in two places:\n"
      "  stroke.color             (only when stroke.paint is the color case)\n"
      "  glow.color\n"
      "The unset-stays-unset rule and the leave-a-gradient-alone rule are\n"
      "identical to recolorShape's.\n"
      "\n"
      "GHOSTING, when and only when `change` is DELETED -- ONE edit:\n"
      "  stroke.dashing is set to STROKE_PATTERN_DOTTED, discarding whatever\n"
      "    dashing it had. If the glyph has no stroke at all, no stroke is\n"
      "    created.\n"
      "There is no second edit here. A Glyph1D has no fill field at all, so\n"
      "the opacity half of recolorShape's ghosting has nothing to act on and\n"
      "no Fill is invented. A deleted edge is therefore dotted but at full\n"
      "strength, which is the most this glyph type can carry.\n"
      "\n"
      "CARRIED THROUGH UNTOUCHED, in full: stroke.width, stroke.cap,\n"
      "stroke.join, glow.radius, glow.intensity, and arrowheads entirely --\n"
      "both variants and the size. Arrowheads have no colour of their own in\n"
      "style.proto, since the renderer paints them from the stroke, so they\n"
      "follow the recoloured stroke without needing a rule."
    inputs: [
      { name: "glyph",     type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.style.v1.Glyph1D" } } },
      { name: "change",    type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } } },
      { name: "diffRoles", type: { named: { symbol: "DiffRoles" } }, is_optional: true }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.style.v1.Glyph1D" } }
    uses: ["diffColorFor", "archeglyph.style.v1.StrokePattern"]
  }
]
